      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Only In Death Does Duty End" id="aab2-95de-b174-0124" hidden="false">
          <description>Once Grimaldus has lost all Wounds (including via Instant Death), take a Leadership test. If passed, Grimaldus fights on with 1 Wound. If failed, remove him from play.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Cenobyte Retinue" id="01fb-2b73-46c6-d885" hidden="false">
          <description>Grimaldus leads 3 Cenobyte Servitors. As long as one is alive, Grimaldus counts as having a Holy Relic.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
  </selectionEntries>
  <sharedInfoGroups>
    <infoGroup name="Vows" id="2992-8995-a4a2-41f7" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Vows" id="579b-f588-4510-78ce" hidden="false">
          <description>The Black Templars must swear one vow before a battle. Choose which vow your army has sword after you&apos;ve determine the mission but before either army sets up.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Vow: Accept Any Challenge, No Matter the Odds" id="69cd-a36e-32d2-49c5" hidden="false">
          <description>All units must assault the enemy if they are in range at the start of the Assault phase, and they must make an advance move if they win a combat, if they would normally be allowed to do so. In close combat, the Black Templars always hit on a 3+, but Neophytes roll using WS as normal.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Vow: Uphold the Honour of the Emperor" id="a97f-88c1-e974-c4ad" hidden="false">
          <description>Black Templar units may not count cover for saving throws or when assaulted, however they gain a 6+ invulnerable saving throw. Neophytes may count cover as normal but do not gain the invulnerable save.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Vow: Suffer Not the Unclean To Live" id="b93d-2b40-f4de-f1bf" hidden="false">
          <description>When rolling to wound in close combat, Black Templars add +1 to their dice roll. A roll of 1 always fails to wound. But to do so, they must now strike at -1 Initiative. Neophytes strike and wound as normal.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Vow: Be Pure in Mind, Body, and Soul" id="eba0-2b27-9c13-c741" hidden="false">
          <description>If an enemy psyker is on the table at the start of the Black Templars&apos; first movement phase, the Black Templars must make an additional move towards the enemy before their normal move. This distance moved is 2D6&quot; (roll for each unit) and each unit must move the full distance, ending the move closer to the enemy than when they started, if possible. After this initial surge, units may make their normal move without restriction. All units count as moving that turn when resolving shooting.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </infoGroup>
  </sharedInfoGroups>
